{
  "abstract": "This corrected successor separates descent of upstairs dynamics, recovery from shadow data, and selection of probability measures. It proves the fiber-preservation criterion for deterministic descent, injectivity on a declared code as the criterion for exact recovery, and reversibility of a quotient when the fiber relation is preserved in both time directions. It also proves that arbitrary finite probability vectors can be represented by basin volumes, so basin representation alone derives neither Born, Hawking nor cosmological weights. Measurement instruments and islands are updates or restricted recovery; a common MTT source remains conditional on one selected upper measure and three explicit pushforwards.",
